WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.588
Log in. Download. Copy. Paste. Send.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.782
Every week, the same clicks.

00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:14.324
What if you only had to explain it once?

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:19.653
Just tell Kitewell your usual work, in your own words.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:25.893
Every step is laid out, so you can check it at a glance.

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:30.950
Then leave the clicking to it.

00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:34.680
Websites, desktop apps, and email.

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:37.430
Even an old app that connects to nothing.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:40.940
Where it matters, it waits for your OK.

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:43.560
Every step is kept on record.

00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:50.295
Excel lists too: it runs each row and writes the results back.

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:53.030
It learns the clicks just once.

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:57.670
Then it repeats them every weekday, without paying for AI.

00:00:57.860 --> 00:01:00.440
Prefer code? Underneath, it's readable YAML.

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:05.210
Run scripts, containers, even Claude Code or Codex.

00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:09.090
Or have your own agent build it, over MCP.

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:11.630
It all runs on your computer.

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:16.280
Share workflows with your team. Your passwords stay with you.

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:17.410
Kitewell.

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:19.400
It flies on its own.

00:01:19.450 --> 00:01:21.340
The string is in your hands.
